    "text": "Tweode gifena in \u00f0ys ginnan grunde.\nHeo \u00f0ar \u00f0a gearwe funde mundbyrd \u00e6t \u00f0am m\u00e6ran \u00feeodne, \u00fea heo ahte m\u00e6ste \u00feearfe, hyldo \u00fe\u00e6s\nHyre \u00f0\u00e6s f\u00e6der on roderum torhtmod ti\u00f0e gefremede, \u00fee heo ahte trumne geleafan a to \u00f0am \u00e6lmihtigan.\nGefr\u00e6gen ic \u00f0a Holofernus winhatan wyrcean georne ond eallum wundrum \u00ferymlic girwan up\nTo \u00f0am het se gumena baldor ealle \u00f0a yldestan \u00f0egnas; hie \u00f0\u00e6t ofstum miclum r\u00e6fndon, rondwiggende,\n\u00de\u00e6t w\u00e6s \u00fey feor\u00f0an dogore \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0e Iudith hyne, gleaw on ge\u00f0once, ides \u00e6lfscinu, \u00e6rest gesohte.\nHie \u00f0a to \u00f0am symle sittan eodon, wlance to wingedrince, ealle his weagesi\u00f0as, bealde byrnwiggende.\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6ron bollan steape boren \u00e6fter bencum gelome, swylce eac bunan ond orcas fulle fletsittendum;\n\u00d0a wear\u00f0 Holofernus, goldwine gumena, on gytesalum, hloh ond hlydde, hlynede ond dynede, \u00fe\u00e6t\nSwa se inwidda ofer ealne d\u00e6g dryhtguman sine drencte mid wine, swi\u00f0mod sinces brytta, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t hie on\nSwa het se gumena aldor fylgan fletsittendum, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t fira bearnum neal\u00e6hte niht seo \u00feystre.\nHet \u00f0a ni\u00f0a geblonden \u00fea eadigan m\u00e6g\u00f0 ofstum fetigan to his bedreste beagum gehl\u00e6ste, hringum\nHie hra\u00f0e fremedon, anbyhtscealcas, swa him heora ealdor bebead, byrnwigena brego, bearhtme stopon\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6s eallgylden fleohnet f\u00e6ger ymbe \u00fe\u00e6s folctogan bed ahongen, \u00fe\u00e6t se bealofulla mihte wlitan\nHie \u00f0a on reste gebrohton snude \u00f0a snoteran idese; eodon \u00f0a stercedferh\u00f0e, h\u00e6le\u00f0 heora hearran cy\u00f0an\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 se brema on mode bli\u00f0e, burga ealdor, \u00feohte \u00f0a beorhtan idese mid widle ond mid womme\nNe wolde \u00fe\u00e6t wuldres dema ge\u00f0afian, \u00ferymmes hyrde, ac he him \u00fe\u00e6s \u00f0inges gestyrde, dryhten, duge\u00f0a\nGewat \u00f0a se deofulcunda, galferh\u00f0 gumena \u00f0reate bealofull his beddes neosan, \u00fe\u00e6r he sceolde his bl\u00e6d\nGefeol \u00f0a wine swa druncen se rica on his reste middan, swa he nyste r\u00e6da nanne on gewitlocan.\nWiggend stopon ut of \u00f0am inne ofstum miclum, weras winsade, \u00fee \u00f0one w\u00e6rlogan, la\u00f0ne leodhatan,\n\u00dea w\u00e6s nergendes \u00feeowen \u00ferymful, \u00feearle gemyndig hu heo \u00feone atolan ea\u00f0ost mihte ealdre ben\u00e6man\nGenam \u00f0a wundenlocc scyppendes m\u00e6g\u00f0 scearpne mece, scurum heardne, ond of scea\u00f0e abr\u00e6d\n\u00deearle ys me nu \u00f0a heorte onh\u00e6ted ond hige geomor, swy\u00f0e mid sorgum gedrefed.\nForgif me, swegles ealdor, sigor ond so\u00f0ne geleafan, \u00fe\u00e6t ic mid \u00feys sweorde mote geheawan \u00feysne\nNahte ic \u00feinre n\u00e6fre miltse \u00feon maran \u00feearfe.\nGewrec nu, mihtig dryhten, torhtmod tires brytta, \u00fe\u00e6t me ys \u00feus torne on mode, hate on hre\u00f0re minum.\nHi \u00f0a se hehsta dema \u00e6dre mid elne onbryrde, swa he de\u00f0 anra gehwylcne herbuendra \u00fee hyne him to\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 hyre rume on mode, haligre hyht geniwod; genam \u00f0a \u00feone h\u00e6\u00f0enan mannan f\u00e6ste be feaxe\nSloh \u00f0a wundenlocc \u00feone feondscea\u00f0an fagum mece, hete\u00feoncolne, \u00fe\u00e6t heo healfne forcearf \u00feone\nN\u00e6s \u00f0a dead \u00fea gyt, ealles orsawle; sloh \u00f0a eornoste ides ellenrof o\u00f0re si\u00f0e \u00feone h\u00e6\u00f0enan hund, \u00fe\u00e6t\nL\u00e6g se fula leap gesne be\u00e6ftan, g\u00e6st ellor hwearf under neowelne n\u00e6s ond \u00f0\u00e6r geny\u00f0erad w\u00e6s, susle\nNe \u00f0earf he hopian no, \u00feystrum for\u00f0ylmed, \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0onan mote of \u00f0am wyrmsele, ac \u00f0\u00e6r wunian sceal\nH\u00e6fde \u00f0a gefohten forem\u00e6rne bl\u00e6d Iudith \u00e6t gu\u00f0e, swa hyre god u\u00f0e, swegles ealdor, \u00fee hyre sigores\n\u00dea seo snotere m\u00e6g\u00f0 snude gebrohte \u00fe\u00e6s herew\u00e6\u00f0an heafod swa blodig on \u00f0am f\u00e6telse \u00fee hyre\nEodon \u00f0a gegnum \u00feanonne \u00fea idesa ba ellen\u00feriste, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t hie becomon, collenferh\u00f0e, eadhre\u00f0ige\nHie \u00f0a beahhrodene fe\u00f0elaste for\u00f0 onettan, o\u00f0 hie gl\u00e6dmode gegan h\u00e6fdon to \u00f0am wealgate.\nWiggend s\u00e6ton, weras w\u00e6ccende wearde heoldon in \u00f0am f\u00e6stenne, swa \u00f0am folce \u00e6r geomormodum\nW\u00e6s \u00f0a eft cumen leof to leodum, ond \u00f0a lungre het gleawhydig wif gumena sumne of \u00f0\u00e6re ginnan\nEow ys metod bli\u00f0e, cyninga wuldor; \u00fe\u00e6t gecy\u00f0ed wear\u00f0 geond woruld wide, \u00fe\u00e6t eow ys wuldorbl\u00e6d\n\u00dea wurdon bli\u00f0e burhsittende, sy\u00f0\u00f0an hi gehyrdon hu seo halige spr\u00e6c ofer heanne weall.\nHere w\u00e6s on lustum.\nWi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s f\u00e6stengeates folc onette, weras wif somod, wornum ond heapum, \u00f0reatum ond \u00f0rymmum\n\u00c6ghwylcum wear\u00f0 men on \u00f0\u00e6re medobyrig mod areted, sy\u00f0\u00f0an hie ongeaton \u00fe\u00e6t w\u00e6s Iudith cumen\n\u00dea seo gleawe het, golde gefr\u00e6tewod, hyre \u00f0inenne \u00feancolmode \u00fe\u00e6s herew\u00e6\u00f0an heafod onwri\u00f0an ond\nSpr\u00e6c \u00f0a seo \u00e6\u00f0ele to eallum \u00feam folce: Her ge magon sweotole sigerofe h\u00e6le\u00f0, leoda r\u00e6swan, on\nNu ic gumena gehw\u00e6ne \u00feyssa burgleoda biddan wylle, randwiggendra, \u00fe\u00e6t ge recene eow fysan to\nSy\u00f0\u00f0an frym\u00f0a god, arf\u00e6st cyning, eastan sende leohtne leoman, bera\u00f0 linde for\u00f0, bord for breostum\nFynd syndon eowere gedemed to dea\u00f0e, ond ge dom agon, tir \u00e6t tohtan, swa eow getacnod hafa\u00f0\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 snelra werod snude gegearewod, cenra to campe.\nStopon cynerofe secgas ond gesi\u00f0as, b\u00e6ron sige\u00feufas, foron to gefeohte for\u00f0 on gerihte, h\u00e6le\u00f0 under\nDynedan scildas, hlude hlummon.\n\u00de\u00e6s se hlanca gefeah wulf in walde, ond se wanna hrefn, w\u00e6lgifre fugel.\nWistan begen \u00fe\u00e6t him \u00f0a \u00feeodguman \u00feohton tilian fylle on f\u00e6gum; ac him fleah on last earn \u00e6tes\nStopon hea\u00f0orincas, beornas to beadowe, bordum be\u00f0eahte, hwealfum lindum, \u00fea \u00f0e hwile \u00e6r\nHim \u00fe\u00e6t hearde wear\u00f0 \u00e6t \u00f0am \u00e6scplegan eallum forgolden, Assyrium, sy\u00f0\u00f0an Ebreas under\nHie \u00f0a fromlice leton for\u00f0 fleogan flana scuras, hilden\u00e6dran, of hornbogan, str\u00e6las stedehearde;\nH\u00e6le\u00f0 w\u00e6ron yrre, landbuende, la\u00f0um cynne, stopon styrnmode, stercedferh\u00f0e, wrehton unsofte\nSwa \u00f0a mago\u00feegnas on \u00f0a morgentid ehton el\u00f0eoda ealle \u00ferage, o\u00f0\u00fe\u00e6t ongeaton \u00f0a \u00f0e grame w\u00e6ron,\nHie wordum \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feam yldestan ealdor\u00feegnum cy\u00f0an eodon, wrehton cumbolwigan ond him forhtlice\n\u00dea ic \u00e6dre gefr\u00e6gn slegef\u00e6ge h\u00e6le\u00f0 sl\u00e6pe tobredon ond wi\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6s bealofullan burgeteldes werigferh\u00f0e\nHogedon aninga hyra hlaforde hilde bodian, \u00e6r\u00f0on \u00f0e him se egesa on ufan s\u00e6te, m\u00e6gen Ebrea.\nMynton ealle \u00fe\u00e6t se beorna brego ond seo beorhte m\u00e6g\u00f0 in \u00f0am wlitegan tr\u00e6fe w\u00e6ron \u00e6tsomne,\nN\u00e6s \u00f0eah eorla nan \u00fee \u00f0one wiggend aweccan dorste o\u00f0\u00f0e gecunnian hu \u00f0one cumbolwigan wi\u00f0 \u00f0a\nM\u00e6gen neal\u00e6hte, folc Ebrea, fuhton \u00feearle heardum heoruw\u00e6pnum, h\u00e6fte guldon hyra fyrngeflitu,\nBeornas stodon ymbe hyra \u00feeodnes tr\u00e6f \u00feearle gebylde, sweorcendferh\u00f0e.\nHi \u00f0a somod ealle ongunnon cohhetan, cirman hlude ond gristbitian, gode orfeorme, mid to\u00f0on torn\n\u00dea w\u00e6s hyra tires \u00e6t ende, eades ond ellend\u00e6da.\nHogedon \u00fea eorlas aweccan hyra winedryhten; him wiht ne speow.\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 si\u00f0 ond late sum to \u00f0am arod \u00feara beadorinca, \u00fe\u00e6t he in \u00fe\u00e6t burgeteld ni\u00f0heard ne\u00f0de, swa\nFunde \u00f0a on bedde blacne licgan his goldgifan g\u00e6stes gesne, lifes belidenne.\nHe \u00fea lungre gefeoll freorig to foldan, ongan his feax teran, hreoh on mode, ond his hr\u00e6gl somod, ond\nHer li\u00f0 sweorde geheawen, beheafdod healdend ure.\nHi \u00f0a hreowigmode wurpon hyra w\u00e6pen of dune, gewitan him werigferh\u00f0e on fleam sceacan.\nHim mon feaht on last, m\u00e6geneacen folc, o\u00f0 se m\u00e6sta d\u00e6l \u00fe\u00e6s heriges l\u00e6g hilde ges\u00e6ged on \u00f0am\nFlugon \u00f0a \u00f0e lyfdon, la\u00f0ra lindwerod.\nHim on laste for sweot Ebrea sigore geweor\u00f0od, dome gedyrsod; him feng dryhten god f\u00e6gre on\nHi \u00f0a fromlice fagum swyrdum, h\u00e6le\u00f0 higerofe, herpa\u00f0 worhton \u00feurh la\u00f0ra gemong, linde heowon,\nSceotend w\u00e6ron gu\u00f0e gegremede, guman Ebrisce; \u00feegnas on \u00f0a tid \u00feearle gelyste gargewinnes.\n\u00de\u00e6r on greot gefeoll se hyhsta d\u00e6l heafodgerimes Assiria ealdordugu\u00f0e, la\u00f0an cynnes.\nLythwon becom cwicera to cy\u00f0\u00f0e.\nCirdon cynerofe, wiggend on wi\u00f0ertrod, w\u00e6lscel on innan, reocende hr\u00e6w.\nRum w\u00e6s to nimanne londbuendum on \u00f0am la\u00f0estan, hyra ealdfeondum unlyfigendum heolfrig\nH\u00e6fdon domlice on \u00f0am folcstede fynd oferwunnen e\u00f0elweardas, ealdhettende swyrdum aswefede.\nHie on swa\u00f0e reston, \u00fea \u00f0e him to life la\u00f0ost w\u00e6ron cwicera cynna.\n\u00dea seo cneoris eall, m\u00e6g\u00f0a m\u00e6rost, anes mon\u00f0es fyrst, wlanc, wundenlocc, wagon ond l\u00e6ddon to\nEal \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0a \u00f0eodguman \u00ferymme geeodon, cene under cumblum on compwige \u00feurh Iudithe gleawe lare,\nHi to mede hyre of \u00f0am si\u00f0fate sylfre brohton, eorlas \u00e6scrofe, Holofernes sweord ond swatigne helm,\nEalles \u00f0\u00e6s Iudith s\u00e6gde wuldor weroda dryhtne, \u00fee hyre weor\u00f0mynde geaf, m\u00e6r\u00f0e on moldan rice,\n\u00d0\u00e6s sy \u00f0am leofan drihtne wuldor to widan aldre, \u00fee gesceop wind ond lyfte, roderas ond rume",
